{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"cd93b871-2f1f-42be-8a9b-f74dae7462bb","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Implemented a two‑segment cache control for the system prompt:\n\n- **`build_system`** now returns two separate `ephemeral` cache blocks:\n  1. **Static instructions** (unchanging, stays hot in cache).\n  2. **Per‑athlete context** (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language) that can be re‑cached after a `save_fact` without evicting the static block.\n\n- Added a comprehensive docstring explaining the rationale and how it aligns with Anthropic’s prefix‑hash caching.\n\nThe full description of the changes and the parts of the colleague’s note that were utilized are recorded in **[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/cd93b871-2f1f-42be-8a9b-f74dae7462bb/ANSWER.md)**.\n","duration_seconds":47.091358,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":20135,"output_tokens":3234,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":180992,"total_tokens":23369}}}
